# rust-analyzer

This project already has rust-analyzer in the editor. Every turn may use that same session through the workspace diagnostic read (`ReadLints`). Do not start a second analyzer, and do not add an extra MCP.

The agent decides whether to use those diagnostics. Use them after a Rust edit when the question is a type, borrow, visibility, unused item, or unresolved import. Skip them when the turn does not edit Rust. A crate-local `cargo check -p <crate>` is the fallback when the diagnostic list is empty.

Keep StoryOS-owned `make verify` and targeted repository checks for format, SQL, HTTP, persistence, and browser journeys. rust-analyzer cannot see those.
